 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection algorithm in MATLAB, you need to add an extra step to your code. Here's how you can modify your existing code to include a Gaussian filter:
```matlab
% Read input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Define Gaussian filter (standard deviation is 1)
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 1);
% Apply Gaussian filter to grayscale image
filtered_image = imfilter(double(gray_image), gaussian_filter, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image, filtered image, and edge image
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image); title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(gray_image); title('Grayscale Image');
subplot(1,3,3), imshow(edge_image); title('Edge Image');
```
This modified code applies a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function before performing Sobel edge detection. The standard deviation of the Gaussian filter is set to 1 in this example, but you can adjust it as needed to control the amount of smoothing applied to the image.

