Question: Write a Java method for creating an OAuth2 access token using Spring Security.

Answer:
1. Import necessary dependencies: `import org.springframework.security.oauth2.common.OAuth2AccessToken;
import org.springframework.security.oauth2.provider.token.TokenStore;`
2. Define method signature: `public OAuth2AccessToken createAccessToken(String tokenType, String accessToken, String refreshToken, long accessTokenExpiration, String authenticatedPrincipal)`
3. Implement method body:
```java
@Autowired
private TokenStore tokenStore;

public OAuth2AccessToken createAccessToken(String tokenType, String accessToken, String refreshToken, long accessTokenExpiration, String authenticatedPrincipal) {
    return tokenStore.readWriteToken(new DefaultAccessToken(accessToken, tokenType, authenticatedPrincipal, accessTokenExpiration, new DefaultRefreshToken(refreshToken), null));
}
```

