 I'd be happy to help you understand the situation you're encountering with your request not including an Authorization header when making an API call. The issue might indeed be related to the 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header, but it's essential to clarify some concepts before diving into specifics.

When making cross-origin requests from a web application, the browser imposes certain security restrictions due to the Same Origin Policy (SOP). One of these restrictions is that the request cannot include credentials like cookies, authorization headers, and client certificates unless the server explicitly allows it by setting the appropriate Access-Control-* headers in its response.

The 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header determines which origins (i.e., URLs) are allowed to access the resource on the server. A value of '*' or wildcard ('\*) means that any origin is allowed, essentially disabling the SOP for this particular resource. However, even if this header is set to '*', it does not automatically enable the inclusion of credentials in the request.

To allow the inclusion of credentials like the Authorization header, the server must also set the following headers:

1. 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials': true
2. 'Access-Control-Expose-Headers': 'Authorization' (if the Authorization header contains sensitive information)

So, in summary, if you're unable to include the Authorization header in your request, check whether the server sets the required Access-Control-Allow-Credentials header to true and the 'Access-Control-Expose-Headers' header to 'Authorization'. If it doesn't, then the server needs to be updated accordingly.

If you have control over the server-side code, you can update the headers as follows:

For Node.js using Express:
```javascript
app.use(function(req, res, next) {
  // Enable CORS and expose Authorization header
  res.header("Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "*");
  res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', true);
  res.header("Access-Control-Expose-Headers", "Authorization");
  next();
});
```

